+          // 2. Task 1 has some other component that reads from the DOM in a
+          //    layout effect or ref (e.g. `useLifecycleRef()`, refs run during
+          //    the React layout phase). This could be a `<Tooltip>` or
+          //    `<VirtualizedScrollView>` or anything really. It's by design that
+          //    you can read from the DOM in a layout effect or ref. Anyway, this
+          //    read forces a browser layout.
+          // 3. Task 2 has ProseMirror add its editor to the DOM in a layout effect
+          // 4. Task 2 has some other component that reads from the DOM which
+          //    forces another browser layout.
+          // 5. So on for all remaining tasks...
+          //
+          // Given layout thrashing is expensive we want to batch our mutations
